{"id": "DeTVlJzxleH", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why did Ravana have TEN heads? 😳 Imagine brushing 320 teeth with ONE mirror… 🪞😂\n\nBut here's the real story!\n\nIn the Uttara Kanda of the Valmiki Ramayana, Ravana performed tapasya for 10,000 years, offering one of his heads into the sacred fire every 1,000 years.\n\nJust before he could offer his last head, Brahma appeared! He restored Ravana's heads and granted him a boon: protection from gods, demons and celestial beings.\n\nHumans? Ravana didn't bother asking for protection from them. He thought they were too insignificant to pose a threat. 🌱\n\nGuess who was human?\n\nRAMA 🏹🔥\n\nAnd there's another popular interpretation of Ravana's ten heads…\n\nThey represent ten human weaknesses we must overcome: ego, anger, greed, jealousy, pride, attachment, selfishness, injustice, cruelty and other flaws.\n\nThat's why Dussehra reminds us that even the mightiest can fall when their flaws take over. 🔥\n\n📚 Love stories from India's rich heritage? Explore the Rishi Katha picture books!\n\nBooks 1–3: Shailputri, Brahmacharini & Chandraghanta.\n\nSet of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n👇 Which head are YOU in the morning?\n\n😴 SLEEPY \n🍕 HUNGRY \n😡 ANGRY\n\nComment below! Save this for Dussehra and send it to your sleepiest friend 😂\n\n#Ravana #Dussehra #Dussehra2026 #Ramayana #Ravan #JaiShriRam #Vijayadashami #IndianMythology #HinduMythology #MythologyForKids #KidsStories #FunnyReels #IndianKids #RishiKatha #PictureBooks", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1791610331, "like_count": 7627, "comment_count": 35, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2351596205651870a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 55.897, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNQC2pVG